{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 30, "model_name": "abacusai/dracarys-llama-3.1-70b-instruct", "content": "Raymond III Count of Tripoli was a Count of Tripoli from 1152 to 1187. He was the son of Raymond II and Hodierna of Jerusalem. Raymond III was a member of the House of Toulouse and a cousin of King Baldwin III of Jerusalem.\n\n**Early Life and Reign**\nRaymond III was born around 1140. His father Raymond II was a Count of Tripoli and his mother Hodierna was a daughter of Baldwin II of Jerusalem. Raymond III was still a minor when his father was murdered in 1152. The regency was held by his mother Hodierna who ruled until 1155 when Raymond III came of age.\n\n*War with Nur ad-Din*\nIn 1164 Raymond III was captured by Nur ad-Din during the Battle of Artah. He was released in 1165 after a ransom was paid. In 1167 Raymond III allied with King Amalric I of Jerusalem to attack Nur ad-Din but the alliance was unsuccessful. Raymond III also allied with the Byzantine Empire to attack Nur ad-Din but the alliance was also unsuccessful.\n\n**Marriage and Family**\nRaymond III married Eschiva of Bures in 1174. Eschiva was a daughter of Walter of Bures and a member of the House of Bures. Raymond III and Eschiva had no children together.\n\n**Later Life and Death**\nRaymond III died on September 6 1187. He was succeeded by his cousin Raymond IV of Tripoli. Raymond III was a member of the House of Toulouse and a cousin of King Baldwin III of Jerusalem. He was a Count of Tripoli from 1152 to 1187 and played an important role in the politics of the Kingdom of Jerusalem during his reign.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Ray", "logprob": -0.0042625186033546925}, {"token": "mond", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " III", "logprob": -6.9141628955549095e-06}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.30444204807281494}, {"token": " of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": -3.814704541582614e-06}, {"token": "oli", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " was", "logprob": -0.01566673